*** 26.3.0 features

- Remote history queries from :tool:`condor_history` **-name** and the new
  ``users``, ``jobs``, ``batchnames``, ``batchids``, and ``dagids`` filters of
  :meth:`htcondor2.Schedd.history` can now use the :ref:`archive-librarian`
  database.
  :jira:`4006`

*** 26.3.0 bugs

- Remote history queries are now answered as the condor user instead of root.
  :jira:`4006`

- Removed support for the SGE (Sun/Oracle Grid Engine) batch system from
  the **batch** grid :subcom:`universe` and :tool:`condor_remote_cluster`.
  The ``sge`` grid type and ``batch sge`` grid resource are no longer
  accepted.
  :jira:`4100`

- When :tool:`condor_ssh_to_job` cannot enter a Singularity or Apptainer
  container job, it now prints an error saying which step failed and the
  likely cause, rather than always blaming a setuid container runtime,
  and exits with a non-zero status.  Also, when running a command in a
  Singularity or Apptainer job, :tool:`condor_ssh_to_job` now exits with
  the exit status of that command, rather than always exiting with zero.
  :jira:`4060`

*** 26.3.0 bugs

*** 26.0.3 bugs

- Fixed a rare bug that would cause the *condor_procd*, and then
  all other daemons to hang. This would only happen on systems
  that do not use cgroups.  That is, glideins, personal condors,
  and other non-root Linux systems.
  :jira:`4105`

- Fixed an unlikely bug where if a local universe starter crashes,
  the *condor_schedd* now cleans up the job's scratch directory
  immediately at job exit time, instead of waiting for the *condor_schedd*
  to restart.
  :jira:`4096`

*** 26.2.0 features

- Administrators can now cap the DAGMan throttles that users may set via
  new configuration options such as :macro:`DAGMAN_MAX_JOBS_IDLE_CEILING`
  and :macro:`DAGMAN_USER_LOG_SCAN_INTERVAL_FLOOR`. These options may only
  be set in the HTCondor system configuration. DAGMan will exit with an error
  if they are set via :macro:`USER_CONFIG_FILE` or ``_CONDOR_`` environment
  variables, and ignores them in a DAG specific configuration file.
  :jira:`3963`

- The :tool:`htcondor annex` commands *create* and *add* are now treated
  equivalently and can be issued before any jobs for the named annex have
  been submitted.
  :jira:`3931`

- Docker Universe jobs on AMD GPU machines should now be able to see 
  the AMD GPU devices.
  :jira:`4047`

- When running as root on a cgroup v2 system, if a GPU job is allocated
  an NVIDIA MIG device, hide all the GPUs not part of the allocated MIGs.
  :jira:`3978`

- Enhance :tool:`condor_gpu_discovery` to publish MIG-specific
  gpu attributes when running on a mig-enabled NVidia gpu.
  :jira:`3978`

- Add submit commands for **batch** grid :subcom:`universe` jobs to
  specify the number of cpus and machines for the job:
  :subcom:`batch_cpu_count`, :subcom:`batch_node_count`,
  :subcom:`batch_cpus_per_node`, and :subcom:`batch_whole_nodes`.
  Setting :subcom:`request_cpus` to a value greater than ``1`` is now
  equivalent to setting :subcom:`batch_cpu_count` to the given value and
  setting :subcom:`batch_node_count` to ``1``.
  :jira:`4053`

- :tool:`condor_gpu_discovery` now publishes a ``Vendor`` property
  for each GPU, such as ``"NVIDIA"`` or ``"AMD"``, so that jobs and
  HTCondor itself can tell GPU types apart.
  :jira:`4007`

- When running Docker universe jobs, the execute event is now logged
  when the container is *started*, not when it is *created*.  The
  container start may take some time, so this makes various statistics
  more accurate, and allows :tool:`condor_ssh_to_job` to have a better
  idea when the container is actually running.
  :jira:`3966`

- Docker universe jobs now have :ad-attr:`DockerImageHash` recorded
  in the job ad for provenance reasons.
  :jira:`974`

- The shared-port id of the primary daemons (i.e. the master and its
  immediate children) now matches their name in the ``DAEMON_LIST`` and
  don't change when the daemons restart.
  :jira:`3984`

- The *condor_shadow* now sets :ad-attr:`JobReconnectedDate` to the current
  time in the job ad whenever it successfully reconnects to the
  *condor_starter*.
  :jira:`4013`

- :tool:`condor_history` and :tool:`condor_q` now include :ad-attr:`JobBatchName`,
  :ad-attr:`DAGNodeName`, :ad-attr:`JobStartDate`, :ad-attr:`JobCurrentStartExecutingDate`,
  :ad-attr:`NumJobCompletions` in the resulting ClassAds generated from a
  user log provided by the ``-userlog`` option.
  :jira:`4081`

- The *condor_starter* now advertises :ad-attr:`HasCgroup` as ``True``
  when jobs on that execution point will be placed in a per-job cgroup.
  The ``CgroupEnforced`` attribute, which the *condor_startd*
  advertised in the slot ad of a running job, has been removed.
  :jira:`3995`

- The job ad now includes :ad-attr:`ActivationRequestMemory`, the value
  :ad-attr:`RequestMemory` evaluated to when the job's most recent
  activation started, so the memory each activation actually requested
  is recorded in the job epoch history and the job history even when
  :ad-attr:`RequestMemory` is an expression.
  :jira:`4062`

- The job ad now includes :ad-attr:`CurrentWastedMemoryGBHours`, the
  gigabyte-hours of requested but unused memory so far in the job's
  current activation, updated as the job runs, and
  :ad-attr:`LastWastedMemoryGBHours`, its final value for the most
  recent activation to have ended.
  :jira:`4062`
  
- Added new submit commands :subcom:`organized_output`, :subcom:`organized_output_directory`
  and :subcom:`organized_output_pattern` which is a simplified way to put the output
  of the jobs in a joblist into a separate subdirectory for each job.
  :jira:`3618`

- :tool:`condor_history` now accepts ``-dagid``, ``-batchid``, and ``-batchname``
  to query all jobs belonging to a DAGMan workflow or job batch. These queries
  use the :ref:`archive-librarian` database when available.
  :jira:`4041`

*** 26.2.0 bugs

- Fix several bugs that causes :ad-attr:`CPUsUsage` to be incorrect
  while the job was running.  It was always correct in the history
  file.
  :jira:`4044`

- Removed the old DAG file parser and the ``DAGMAN_USE_OLD_FILE_PARSER``
  config knob from *condor_dagman* and :tool:`condor_submit_dag`.
  :jira:`3971`

- Fixed a bug that caused file transfer to fail when the AP and EP had
  different preferences for whether to use IPv4 or IPv6.
  :jira:`4101`

- Fixed a bug where HTCondor would use IPv4 to initiate a network
  connection despite configuration parameter :macro:`ENABLE_IPV4`
  being set to ``False``, and likewise for IPv6.
  :jira:`3970`

*** 26.0.2 bugs

- :tool:`condor_tail` should now work on files larger than 2 Gb in size.
  :jira:`4008`

- Fixed a bug in :macro:`ENVIRONMENT_FOR_Assigned<name>` where it did 
  not replace the matched text. 
  :jira:`4052`

- Fixed several bugs that prevented OCU claims from being made.
  :jira:`4073

- The kernel tuning script run by the :tool:`condor_master` (see
  :macro:`ENABLE_KERNEL_TUNING`) now sets ``/proc/sys/vm/dirty_bytes``
  to 100 MB only on cgroup v1 machines that run a *condor_startd*.
  This limit was a workaround for jobs being OOM killed for writing
  files under cgroup v1, which cgroup v2 does not need, and it could
  greatly slow down file writes, especially to FUSE filesystems such as
  those used by Apptainer.  Machines where the limit was already set
  keep it until reboot.  The new configuration knob
  :macro:`KERNEL_TUNING_LIMIT_DIRTY_BYTES` sets the limit on any
  machine, for rare cgroup v2 cases that still need it.
  :jira:`4065`

- The Python bindings often construct :py:class:`classad2.ClassAd` objects
  using Python's C API.  Previously, the bindings always assumed that the
  constructor would be successful, but it turns out that even an otherwise-successful
  construction can raise an exception if interrupted by a signal, like the
  one generated by hitting ``CTRL+C`` to exit :tool:`condor_watch_q`.
  The bindings no longer always assume success, and you should see crashes
  when doing so much less frequently.  We're working on a complete fix.
  :jira:`4076`

*** 26.1.0 features

- Added :tool:`htcondor cluster`, which caches a cluster's job data
  locally and profiles it to produce a health report, flagging problems
  such as inefficient resource usage or held jobs and recommending
  specific follow-up commands to investigate them.
  :jira:`3892`

- :tool:`condor_gpu_discovery` now advertises an :ad-attr:`Integrated`
  attribute that is true for NVIDIA GPUs that share their memory with the
  host, such as unified-memory devices like the NVIDIA DGX Spark.
  :jira:`3899`

- The DAGMan Node Status File now reports aggregate job proc counts
  (submitted, running, idle, held, completed, and failed) for the DAG
  and each node, and can be written in JSON format.
  :jira:`3928`

- :tool:`condor_history` will now directly locate and read job records
  for a specified :ad-attr:`Owner` or :ad-attr:`ClusterId` when the
  Archive Librarian is in use.
  :jira:`3927`

- Add submit command :subcom:`annex_name`, which intendicates that the
  jobs are intended to run on EPs of the named annex.
  Add submit command :subcom:`restrict_to_annex`, which specifies whether
  these jobs can run only on EPs of the named annex, or can also run on
  non-annex EPs.
  Add new configuration parameter :macro:`ANNEX_RESTRICT_JOB_DEFAULT`,
  which sets the default value for :subcom:`restrict_to_annex`.
  :jira:`2015`

- The Archive Librarian now removes users from its database once they have
  had no indexed jobs for :macro:`LIBRARIAN_USER_RETENTION_DAYS` days, which
  defaults to 365.
  :jira:`3943`

- The Archive Librarian now writes an address file,
  :macro:`LIBRARIAN_ADDRESS_FILE`, so it can be targeted by tools such as
  :tool:`condor_restart` with ``-daemon librarian``.
  :jira:`3943`

- The *condor_starter* can now optionally set a limit on the amount of
  compressed swap (zswap) a job may use, via the new
  :macro:`CGROUP_ZSWAP_MAX_EXPR`. It is a ClassAd expression, evaluated in
  the context of the slot and job ads, whose value in megabytes is written
  to the job's cgroup ``memory.zswap.max``. When it is unset, which is the
  default, HTCondor does not write to that control file at all, and the job
  gets whatever the system default is. Requires cgroup v2 and a kernel with
  zswap support.
  :jira:`3898`

- :tool:`condor_adstash` now includes a ``ndjsonfile`` interface which appends
  JSON per-line to adstash.jsonl in the directory specified by ``--json_dir``.
  :jira:`3959`

- Fixed a bug where the Archive Librarian's garbage collection removed only
  one archive file's records per pass and stopped just under
  :macro:`LIBRARIAN_HIGH_WATER_MARK`, instead of reducing the database to
  :macro:`LIBRARIAN_LOW_WATER_MARK`. Garbage collection also no longer
  mistakes a successful pass for a failed one, which triggered a
  :macro:`LIBRARIAN_GC_BACKOFF_SECONDS` delay, because the database file
  had not yet been checkpointed. The database file on disk now shrinks
  as soon as garbage collection finishes.
  :jira:`3943`

*** 26.1.0 bugs

- To assist in debugging, added :subcom:`min_condor_version` and
  :subcom:`max_condor_version`, which prevent the require the HTCondor
  version of the EP to greater than or equal to, or strictly less than,
  respectively, the specified version, e.g. "26.0.1".
  :jira:`3065`

*** 26.0.1 bugs

- Fixed a bug that incorrectly calculated :ad-attr:`TransferOutQueued`
  :jira:`3987`

- Fixed a rare bug that could cause *condor_dagman* to crash when the
  AP is restarted.
  :jira:`3915`

